{"name":"Chiffon","hex":"#f0f5bb","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chiffon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A lightweight, balanced plain-woven sheer fabric, or gauze, like gossamer, woven of alternate S- and Z-twist crepe (high-twist) yarns made of silk, polyester, or cotton.","Any purely ornamental accessory on a woman's dress, such as a bunch of ribbon, lace, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chiffon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chiffon cake","blocks":[{"text":"A chiffon cake is a light cake made with vegetable oil, eggs, sugar, flour, baking powder, and flavorings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/Meyer_lemon_chiffon_cake%2C_chocolate.jpg/330px-Meyer_lemon_chiffon_cake%2C_chocolate.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiffon_cake"},{"title":"Chiffon (fabric)","blocks":[{"text":"Chiffon, from the French word chiffe which means \"cloth or rag\"; is a lightweight, balanced plain-woven sheer fabric, or gauze, like gossamer, woven of alternate S- and Z-twist crepe (high-twist) yarns. Crepe yarn tends to have a tighter twist than standard yarns. The twist in the crepe yarns puckers the fabric slightly in both directions after weaving, giving it some stretch and a slightly rough feel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Lillian_Gish_2.jpg/330px-Lillian_Gish_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chiffon_(fabric)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Chiffonjf1939.JPG/250px-Chiffonjf1939.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Chiffonjf1939.JPG/500px-Chiffonjf1939.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedi